{
  "description": "Checkout tax parity vectors. The same basket goes through gateway-bff's estimate (app.buildTaxQuote + priceTax) and orders' checkout (CheckoutTaxImpl); both must send tax-returns exactly 'expected.requestLines' for 'shipTo' and must add up the answers to 'expected.taxMinor'. Same request + same tax-returns function = same tax: this pins the first half, the second is tax-returns' own determinism. The fake tax-returns taxes a TAXABLE line at rateBps/10000 of (unit*qty - discount + shipping), rounded half up, and an EXEMPT line at 0. Inputs are the priced basket: 'feeMinor' is the package's delivery fee, 'membershipWaivedMinor' what the membership waives of it, 'shippingDiscountMinor' the coupon's shipping discount over the whole order, taken from the packages in order; a line's 'discountMinor' is its coupon share. 'sellerOrgId' null = AfroTransact's own item. Used by orders (CheckoutTaxParityTest) and gateway-bff (checkout_tax_parity_test.go). The attribution method for mixed baskets is an OPEN LEGAL DECISION (open decision 5).",
